WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.884 --> 00:00:02.672
- [Narrator] General
Tso's Chicken is a staple

00:00:02.672 --> 00:00:04.617
in American Chinese restaurants.

00:00:04.617 --> 00:00:07.103
But the most popular
Chinese dish in the U.S.,

00:00:07.103 --> 00:00:09.603
is virtually unknown in China.

00:00:15.629 --> 00:00:18.129
- [Narrator] So, what happened?

00:00:35.197 --> 00:00:37.266
- [Narrator] It all started
after the Chinese Civil War

00:00:37.266 --> 00:00:40.115
when most of the Chinese
leadership fled to Taiwan.

00:00:40.115 --> 00:00:42.222
The leadership took this guy with them.

00:00:42.222 --> 00:00:44.159
The late Peng Chang-Kuei.

00:00:44.159 --> 00:00:45.558
He was after all the chef to the

00:00:45.558 --> 00:00:47.624
then acting Chinese President.

00:00:47.624 --> 00:00:49.338
On one fateful day there were a bunch

00:00:49.338 --> 00:00:51.921
of foreign dignitaries in town.

00:01:14.249 --> 00:01:16.222
- [Narrator] He named it
that because of General Tso,

00:01:16.222 --> 00:01:19.805
a 19th century hero in
his hometown of Hunan.

00:01:37.502 --> 00:01:39.191
- [Narrator] The dish was
a major hit in Taiwan,

00:01:39.191 --> 00:01:40.667
so he brought it to the United States

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:43.228
and opened up a restaurant.

00:01:43.228 --> 00:01:44.670
Word got out about Peng's restaurant

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:46.833
mainly because the then Secretary of State

00:01:46.833 --> 00:01:51.000
Henry Kissinger was absolutely
bonkers for General Tso's.

00:02:07.079 --> 00:02:08.568
- [Narrator] As with
most successful things,

00:02:08.568 --> 00:02:11.568
people started ripping off the dish.

00:02:29.174 --> 00:02:30.806
- [Narrator] Even though
the General Tso's chicken

00:02:30.806 --> 00:02:33.298
you know and love probably
isn't the real McCoy,

00:02:33.298 --> 00:02:35.010
don't let that stop you from gobbling up

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:38.843
that sweet and spicy,
gooey and crunchy mass.

